    "question": {
      ":question/id": "672ab407-24bd-5001-aed5-7a932548fb74",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1+(2)(4) & 2+(2)(5) & 3+(2)(7) \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 17 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 17 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2+(1)(4) & 6+(1)(5) & 8+(1)(7)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 17 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
